---
const stages = [
  {
    title: 'Just for me',
    consequence: 'I can recreate it.',
    example: 'A disposable personal experiment',
    practice: 'Chat, try it, iterate. No workflow pack or formal test suite required.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Friends or coworkers',
    consequence: 'Others lose time.',
    example: 'A shared tool with saved work',
    practice: 'Check important user journeys, protect saved data, and have a recovery path.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Customers depend on it',
    consequence: 'Failures damage trust.',
    example: 'An application people rely on',
    practice: 'Automate critical checks. Add targeted review, monitoring, and rollback.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Critical service',
    consequence: 'Minutes cause major losses.',
    example: 'An outage can cost thousands a minute',
    practice: 'Set reliability targets. Stage releases, test failures, and practice recovery.',
  },
];
---
<figure class="spectrum" aria-label="Verification grows with the consequences of failure">
  <div class="spectrum-direction">
    <span>Easy to recover</span>
    <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <span>Costly to fail</span>
  </div>
  <ol class="spectrum-stages" role="list">
    {stages.map((stage, i) => (
      <li class="card spectrum-stage">
        <div class="spectrum-meter" aria-hidden="true">
          {[0, 1, 2, 3].map((segment) => <span class:list={{ filled: segment <= i }} />)}
        </div>
        <h3>{stage.title}</h3>
        <p class="spectrum-consequence">{stage.consequence}</p>
        <p class="spectrum-example">{stage.example}</p>
        <p class="spectrum-practice">{stage.practice}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <figcaption>
    Illustrative situations, not mandatory levels. A five-person payroll tool can need stronger
    safeguards than a popular disposable toy. Data sensitivity, recovery difficulty, and the
    change itself matter as much as audience size.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .spectrum { margin: 0; }
  .spectrum-direction { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 16px; color: var(--brand-ink); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.82rem; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .spectrum-direction > :nth-child(2) { flex: 1; text-align: right; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--brand); }
  .spectrum-stages { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .spectrum-stage { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; padding: 22px; min-width: 0; }
  .spectrum-meter { display: flex; gap: 5px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .spectrum-meter span { height: 5px; flex: 1; background: var(--line-strong); border-radius: 2px; }
  .spectrum-meter .filled { background: var(--brand); }
  .spectrum-stage h3 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 0; }
  .spectrum-stage .spectrum-consequence { color: var(--brand-ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .spectrum-stage .spectrum-example { font-size: 0.88rem; }
  .spectrum-practice { border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong); padding-top: 14px; margin-top: auto; }
  figcaption { color: var(--ink-dim); margin-top: 20px; max-width: 85ch; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  @media (max-width: 960px) { .spectrum-stages { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .spectrum-stages { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .spectrum-direction { flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .spectrum-direction > :nth-child(2) { flex: none; border: 0; transform: rotate(90deg); }
  }
</style>
